# Portfolio 5: Distributed and Cloud Database Exercise

## MIVA Master in Information Technology

**Specialisation:** Information Technology Management

## 1. Project Overview

This portfolio explores distributed and cloud database concepts using the Student Management System developed in previous MIVA MIT database portfolios.

The project investigates how distributed database architecture can improve data availability, reliability, scalability, and performance.

## 2. Case Study

The Student Management System manages student records, departments, course registrations, and examination results.

The project explores how these records can be managed across multiple database servers while maintaining data consistency and availability.

## 3. Objectives

- Understand distributed database architecture.
- Implement PostgreSQL replication.
- Explore data consistency and availability.
- Explain database sharding and horizontal scalability.
- Deploy database services using Docker.
- Evaluate distributed database benefits and limitations.

